<title>CANADA: CRICKET-PAKISTAN 170-9 V INDIA.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-PAKISTAN 170-9 V INDIA.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan compiled 170-9 off their 33 overs in the rain-affected one day international against Pakistan at the Toronto Cricket, Skating and Curling club here on Monday.</p>
<p>The first match in the five-game series was reduced to a maximum 33 overs a side after the umpires delayed the start of play due to the damp ground.</p>
<p>Pakistan: 170-9 (Saeed Anwar 46; Javagal Srinath three for 23, Anil Kumble three for 32)</p>
<p>India to bat.</p>
